"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d81\"},\"ref\":\"d81\",\"snippet\":\" ... Since 2005, a second prize, the International Booker Prize, has also been awarded, which since 2016 has gone to the best work in translation.\\n\\nThese 70 judges were 57 percent men; 75 percent English; 16 percent Irish, Scottish, or Welsh; 10 percent other nationalities; and 99 percent white ... \",\"title\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10837049/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d78\"},\"ref\":\"d78\",\"snippet\":\" ... Judas, was shortlisted for the Booker Prize in 2017 and won the Yasnaya Polyana Foreign Fiction Award. He received several international awards, including the Prix Femina, the Israel Prize, the Goethe Prize, the Frankfurt Peace Prize and the 2013 Franz Kafka Prize. He died in 2018 at the ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/30-books-to-celebrate-30-years-of-writers-company-1.5755144\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d9\"},\"ref\":\"d9\",\"snippet\":\" ... Goes Last (2015) (Winner of the 2015 Red Tentacle award)\\n* Hag-Seed (2016) (Longlisted for the 2017 Women Prize for Fiction)\\n* The Testaments (2019, joint winner of the 2019 Booker Prize)\\\"Margaret Atwood announces sequel to The Handmaid's Tale\\\" . CBC News, November 28, 2018.\\n\\n;Short fiction collections ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Atwood\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d90\"},\"ref\":\"d90\",\"snippet\":\" ... Sleeping on Jupiter won the DSC Prize for Fiction 2016 and was longlisted for the Man Booker Prize 2015. All the Lives We Never Lived won the Sahitya Akademi, one of India's highest literary honours, and was shortlisted for the International Dublin Literary Award. It won Tata ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d111\"},\"ref\":\"d111\",\"snippet\":\" ... shortlisted for the Royal Society of Literature Ondaatje Prize and the Women's Prize for Fiction\\n* Swing Time: longlisted for the Man Booker Prize 2017\\n* Granta′s Best of Young British Novelists, 2003 and 2013\\n* 2016: Welt-Literaturpreis\\n* 2017: Langston Hughes Medal\\\"Zadie Smith Wins CCNY's Langston ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zadie_Smith\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d80\"},\"ref\":\"d80\",\"snippet\":\" ... David Cohen Prize for Literature\\n*2011: Man Booker Prize, winner, The Sense of an Ending\\n*2011 Costa Book Awards, shortlist, The Sense of an Ending\\n*2012: Europese Literatuurprijs\\n*2015: Zinklar Award at the first annual Blixen Ceremony in Copenhagen\\n*2016: Siegfried Lenz Prize\\n*2017: Officier in the Ordre ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julian_Barnes\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d112\"},\"ref\":\"d112\",\"snippet\":\" ... for New Writing North's Read Regional campaign 2017 and won the Saboteur Award for Best Novella 2016. My first novel, Sealed (2017), is a work of eco-horror, which was shortlisted for the Not the Booker Award 2018. My second novel, Exit Management (2020), moves between contemporary ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.durham.ac.uk/staff/naomi-r-booth/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d72\"},\"ref\":\"d72\",\"snippet\":\" ... It was also shortlisted for the 2018 Saroyan Prize and longlisted for the 2018 PEN/Robert Bingham Prize for Debut Fiction and the 2017 Story Prize. Her novel The Gone Dead was published by Ecco/HarperCollins in June 2019 and was a New York Times Book Review Editor ... \",\"title\":\"https://artsandsciences.syracuse.edu/english-department/creative-writing-mf-program/raymond-carver-reading-series/previous-raymond-carver-reading-series/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"fb7cccc8ed88ca66465aef3977df9f55215ffb910e5253aafd21d95fc8e0efb1\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"8ba5d04bfc7eb04389c63ac20ae540e505caaf46b6733da56144cd8edd7ae5a9\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Booker International Prize 2016 2017 2018 2019 winner shortlist\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d30\"},\"ref\":\"d30\",\"snippet\":\" ... In a news conference earlier today, International Booker Prize jury chair Frank Wynne credited independent publishers with the lion's share of translated work. \\\"Nobody is surprised that the majority of books on the long- and shortlist,\\\" he said, \\\"are independent publishers. Small independent presses have done enormous ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d91\"},\"ref\":\"d91\",\"snippet\":\" ... The International Booker Prize 2023 Shortlist\\n\\nAt London Book Fair: Insights Into Translation Buyers\\n\\nAs the news of the International Booker Prize shortlist was announced to the public amid the raucous noise and crush of simultaneously programmed events at London Book Fair's opening today (April 17), the ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2023/04/london-book-fair-the-bookers-new-data-on-translation-buyers/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d14\"},\"ref\":\"d14\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2016, the award was significantly reconfigured, and is now given annually to a single book in English translation, with a £50,000 prize for the winning title, shared equally between author and translator. The award has been known as the International Booker Prize since the Man Group ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d90\"},\"ref\":\"d90\",\"snippet\":\" ... His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d113\"},\"ref\":\"d113\",\"snippet\":\" ... Prophet Song by Paul Lynch + Book Club Discussion Guide\\n\\nBooker International Prize\\n\\nA counterpart to the Booker Prize, the International Booker Prize is awarded annually for the finest single work of fiction from around the world that has been translated into English and published in the UK and ... \",\"title\":\"https://bookclubs.com/blog/2023-2024-book-awards-and-book-prize-winners\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d77\"},\"ref\":\"d77\",\"snippet\":\" ... Taylor |\\n| 2003 The Booker Prizes |url= |access-date=2022-10-19 |website=thebookerprizes.com |language=en |archive-date=28 November 2022 |archive-url= |url-status=live }} | Shortlist | Damon Galgut | The Good Doctor | Atlantic Books | *John Carey (Chair) *A. C. Grayling *Francine Stock * Rebecca Stephens MBE *D. J. Taylor ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d110\"},\"ref\":\"d110\",\"snippet\":\" ... of the smallest publisher ever to win the prize, husband-and-wife indie Sort Of Books. In 2022, all the glittering literary prizes went to indies – not only the Booker, but its sister prize for translated fiction, the International Booker, as well as the Nobel, the Goldsmiths, the ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/16/uk-indie-publishing-mavericks-shook-up-books-booker-nobel-fitzcarraldo-sort-of-books-daunt\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d114\"},\"ref\":\"d114\",\"snippet\":\" ... Winner of the 2017 Man Booker International Prize.\\n\\nHerrera explores the crossings and translations people make in their minds and language as they move from one country to another, especially when there's no going back. Traversing this lonely territory is Makina, a young woman who knows only ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.nypl.org/spotlight/world-literature-festival/recommended-translations\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d71\"},\"ref\":\"d71\",\"snippet\":\" ... Publicist Nichola Smalley leaves for a full-time translation career and Michael Watson steps into her shoes.\\n\\n2023\\n\\nPrize attention included a British Book Award shortlisting for Aftermath in the Book of the Year category and the International Booker Prize shortlisting for Eva Baltasar's Boulder (transl. Julia ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.andotherstories.org/about-us/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d27\"},\"ref\":\"d27\",\"snippet\":\" ... Though the most recent Nobel prize in literature winner Han Kang was eligible for this year's prize with her book We Do Not Part, translated from Korean by e. yaewon and Paige Aniyah Morris, she did not make the list. Kang won the International Booker in 2016 ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2025/feb/25/all-13-writers-on-international-booker-longlist-are-first-time-nominees\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"6fcd4903f2df06a2cec874ea750477978c5548b761c41982862fe781e47b9f11\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"9ff074b5891bcdf1fa640f552d42ee1055bb3827b0d7f91138c8307c913f8354\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"book translated 25 languages shortlisted International Booker Prize\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_df97492883bd4777aedb7969"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d115\"},\"ref\":\"d115\",\"snippet\":\" ... Spirits (1982); this work intended to exorcise the ghosts of the Pinochet dictatorship. The book was rejected by numerous Latin American publishers, but eventually published in Barcelona. The book soon ran to more than two dozen editions in Spanish and was translated into a score of languages. Allende ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isabel_Allende\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d116\"},\"ref\":\"d116\",\"snippet\":\" ... This text soon became her debut novel, The House of the Spirits, and that date has become a ceremonial and ritualistic starting point in the creation of all her subsequent works.\\n\\nThe Wandering Spirits of Isabel Allende\\n\\nBy Adán Griego\\n\\nCurator of Latin American and Iberian Collections\\n\\n© 2004 ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.isabelallende.com/en/words/wandering_spirits\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d117\"},\"ref\":\"d117\",\"snippet\":\" ... Isabel Allende has successfully joined the ranks of some of the most distinguished writers of Latin America. She has won praise for her evocative use of language, her style, and her illumination of historical and social reality as well as her ability to entertain. Her works, now known ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.gale.com/intl/databases-explored/literature/isabel-allende\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d118\"},\"ref\":\"d118\",\"snippet\":\" ... In the world I am\\n\\nAlways a stranger\\n\\nI do not understand its language\\n\\nIt does not understand my silence.\\n\\nIt's the birthday of the Chilean novelist Isabel Allende, (books by this author) born in Lima, Peru, in 1942. Her father was a diplomat to Peru, and ... \",\"title\":\"https://writersalmanac.publicradio.org/index.php%3Fdate=2008%252F08%252F02.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d119\"},\"ref\":\"d119\",\"snippet\":\" ... Two of the books were novels originally published in Spanish, though only one was written by a native speaker. I refer to The Wind Knows My Name,[2] by Isabel Allende (born in Peru, raised in Chile) and The Pole,[3] by J. M. Coetzee, the Nobel laureate ... \",\"title\":\"https://hudsonreview.com/2023/10/the-summers-best-fiction-hands-down/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d120\"},\"ref\":\"d120\",\"snippet\":\" ... the novel in its 2005 list of the 100 best English-language novels published since 1923. Read the novel first to see why. Then watch the film starring Halle Berry as the main character, and produced by Oprah Winfrey.\\n\\nHouse of the Spirits by Isabel Allende\\n\\nIsabel Allende ... \",\"title\":\"https://salinapubliclibrary.org/2025/03/off-the-shelf/15-books-to-read-before-watching-the-movie-or-tv-show-according-to-ashley-the-librarian/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d121\"},\"ref\":\"d121\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Memoir of the Senses memorably linked two sections of the bookstore that don't see much crossover: Erotica and Cookbooks. Just as vital is her community work: The Isabel Allende Foundation works with nonprofits in the San Francisco Bay Area and Chile to empower and protect women ... \",\"title\":\"https://mlpp.pressbooks.pub/introductiontohumanitiesv2/chapter/literature-including-fiction-drama-poetry-and-prose/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d122\"},\"ref\":\"d122\",\"snippet\":\" ... For those who wish to seek the original interview, the front cover and table of contents are reproduced at Allende was the first Latin American woman writer recognized outside the continent. Her best-known novel, The House of the Spirits, is arguably similar to García Márquez's style ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magical_realism\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d123\"},\"ref\":\"d123\",\"snippet\":\" ... My Way of Speaking\\n* Emory Elliott for Columbia Literary History of the United States\\n* Eduardo Galeano for Genesis\\n* Frank Chin for The Chinaman Pacific and Frisco R.R. Co.\\n* Henry Louis Gates for The Signifying Monkey: A Theory of Afro-American Literary Criticism\\n* Isabel Allende for Eva Luna ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Book_Awards\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d124\"},\"ref\":\"d124\",\"snippet\":\" ... Pan's Labyrinth (El laberinto del fauno in its original language, which translates directly as \\\"The Labyrinth of the Faun\\\" rather than the singular name of Ancient Greek deity \\\"Pan\\\") wasn't Mexican-born director's first movie. It was actually his fifth, coming after Cronos, Mimic, The ... \",\"title\":\"https://medium.com/@breavous/in-the-vision-of-guillermo-del-toros-magical-realism-and-universal-symbolism-c4ce8c5ed48e\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"60637b502a86bc455359166ea49023b357738d4b4e936c6c69664750ce940636\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"56b6d6bbc2d8c8b1a89be467fa386e71437bcb3cf81dbec88ed46d5c82ee9054\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"The Labyrinth of the Spirits Isabel Allende translated languages\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d115\"},\"ref\":\"d115\",\"snippet\":\" ... Fluent in English, Allende was granted United States citizenship in 1993, having lived in California since 1989.\\n\\nEarly life\\n\\nAllende was born in Lima, Peru, in 1942, the daughter of Francisca Llona Barros called \\\"Doña Panchita\\\" (the daughter of Agustín Llona Cuevas and Isabel Barros Moreira, of Portuguese ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isabel_Allende\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d118\"},\"ref\":\"d118\",\"snippet\":\" ... It's the birthday of the Chilean novelist Isabel Allende, (books by this author) born in Lima, Peru, in 1942. Her father was a diplomat to Peru, and his cousin was Salvador Allende, who later became the first elected socialist president of Chile. Isabel's father left when ... \",\"title\":\"https://writersalmanac.publicradio.org/index.php%3Fdate=2008%252F08%252F02.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d125\"},\"ref\":\"d125\",\"snippet\":\" ... Throughout the 1960s and 1970s military authoritarian regimes ruled in Argentina, Brazil, Chile, Paraguay, Peru and many others. For example, on September 11, 1973, the democratically elected President Salvador Allende was overthrown in Chile and replaced by General Augusto Pinochet, who went on to rule until the end ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latin_American_Boom\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d117\"},\"ref\":\"d117\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2025-01-01\\n---\\nAllende was born in Lima, Peru, on 2 August 1942 to Chilean diplomat Tomás Allende and his wife Francisca Llona Barros. Her father was a first cousin of Salvador Allende, president of Chile, with whom Isabel and her family maintained a close, long-standing relationship ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.gale.com/intl/databases-explored/literature/isabel-allende\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d116\"},\"ref\":\"d116\",\"snippet\":\" ... The Wandering Spirits of Isabel Allende\\n\\nBy Adán Griego\\n\\nCurator of Latin American and Iberian Collections\\n\\n© 2004 Stanford Libraries\\n\\nLike many of her fictional characters, Isabel Allende has spent her life traveling to and living in many places. She was born to diplomat parents in Lima in 1942 ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.isabelallende.com/en/words/wandering_spirits\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d121\"},\"ref\":\"d121\",\"snippet\":\" ... Listen to Isabel Allende's Ted Talk\\n\\nAs a novelist and memoirist, Isabel Allende writes of passionate lives, including her own. Born into a Chilean family with political ties, she went into exile in the United States in the 1970s—an event that, she believes, created her as ... \",\"title\":\"https://mlpp.pressbooks.pub/introductiontohumanitiesv2/chapter/literature-including-fiction-drama-poetry-and-prose/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d119\"},\"ref\":\"d119\",\"snippet\":\" ... I refer to The Wind Knows My Name,[2] by Isabel Allende (born in Peru, raised in Chile) and The Pole,[3] by J. M. Coetzee, the Nobel laureate from South Africa. Coetzee says