nship: Chile, United States\\nspouses ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isabel_Allende\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d116\"},\"ref\":\"d116\",\"snippet\":\" ... The Wandering Spirits of Isabel Allende\\n\\nBy Adán Griego\\n\\nCurator of Latin American and Iberian Collections\\n\\n© 2004 Stanford Libraries\\n\\nLike many of her fictional characters, Isabel Allende has spent her life traveling to and living in many places. She was born to diplomat parents in Lima in 1942 ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.isabelallende.com/en/words/wandering_spirits\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d118\"},\"ref\":\"d118\",\"snippet\":\" ... It's the birthday of the Chilean novelist Isabel Allende, (books by this author) born in Lima, Peru, in 1942. Her father was a diplomat to Peru, and his cousin was Salvador Allende, who later became the first elected socialist president of Chile. Isabel's father left when ... \",\"title\":\"https://writersalmanac.publicradio.org/index.php%3Fdate=2008%252F08%252F02.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d130\"},\"ref\":\"d130\",\"snippet\":\" ... Isabel Allende (1942- ), niece of former Chilean president Salvador\\n\\nAllende, is one of todays most prominent Chilean writers. She has lived many years in\\n\\nCalifornia, having lived abroad ever since the 1973 coup that deposed her uncle. Her fictio...\\n\\nJacques dAmboise (1934- ), recognized as one of the finest ... \",\"title\":\"http://cls.matrix.msu.edu/celebrity-lectures/index.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d131\"},\"ref\":\"d131\",\"snippet\":\" ... His lush prose and intricate storytelling have set the standard for magical realist literature.\\n\\n-\\n\\n-\\n\\nIsabel Allende:\\n\\n-\\n\\nAllende, a Chilean-American author, has made significant contributions to magical realism with works like \\\"The House of the Spirits.\\\" Her storytelling skills and incorporation of magical elements into family sagas have ... \",\"title\":\"https://blueroseone.com/publish/magical-realism/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d132\"},\"ref\":\"d132\",\"snippet\":\" ... From 2009 to 2012, the Library of Congress Creative Achievement\\n\\nAward for fiction was presented to John Grisham, Isabel Allende, Toni\\n\\nMorrison and Philip Roth. Beginning in 2013, the Library of Congress Prize\\n\\nfor American Fiction has been presented to an author for a body of extraordinary\\n\\nwork ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.loc.gov/programs/poetry-and-literature/prizes/fiction-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d119\"},\"ref\":\"d119\",\"snippet\":\" ... Isabel Allende won't get canceled in the way Jeanine Cummins did, and Wind will do some real world good, even if it isn't Allende's best novel.\\n\\nHappily for readers, I do think Tom Lake[4] is Ann Patchett's best novel. I read it on ... \",\"title\":\"https://hudsonreview.com/2023/10/the-summers-best-fiction-hands-down/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d16\"},\"ref\":\"d16\",\"snippet\":\" ... Isabel Allende\\n*2019: Edmund White\\n*2020: Walter Mosley\\n*2021: Karen Tei Yamashita\\n*2022: Art Spiegelman\\n*2023: Rita Dove\\n*2024: Barbara Kingsolver\\n\\nFive of the seventeen medalists through 2004 were previous National Book Award winners (Bellow, Welty, McCullough, Updike, and Roth, all but McCullough for fiction). Between 2005 and ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Book_Award\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"b1e12328164b3a52d18b3dd60ed98e24eae093714c9257642e1f84393aabb908\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"d919b2c0bb77ff8994813605f109cbdb80141e13c96fe4b76b82f17e6a5d8339\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Isabel Allende birthplace biography\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_4e661ade900b4b318c84aa3c"},{"content":"I notice the search results mention Chigozie Obioma's novels \"The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019)\" being \"shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages.\" This is a strong lead. Let me investigate this connection.\n\nThe Booker Prize was created in 1968/1969, not the 2000s. But the puzzle says \"originally created in the 2000s (the award itself).\" Let me reconsider — maybe the award is the International Booker Prize (created 2004/2005). Let me check Obioma's books and the International Booker Prize.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d90\"}","name":"read"},"id":"call_76bff0524f7149cca3bf0789","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Chigozie Obioma The Fishermen International Booker Prize shortlist 2015\", \"An Orchestra of Minorities International Booker Prize 2019 shortlist\", \"Chigozie Obioma born Akure Nigeria biography\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_8cc75fb802434092b09c3038","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d90\",\"document_chars\":17355,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"79767844ce2071fc5dcf3fb0e64d0cade0ba154ef0fc324d0054c1c767e63138\",\"snapshot\":\"90019ca46504785f620ef12f36abae20080c8c3bc7809053339e4beaa4deb2fd\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: ADVISORS\\ndate: 2022-01-01\\n---\\nADVISORS\\n\\nAdvisors\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was named one of Foreign Policy's 100 Leading Global Thinkers in 2015 and served as a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Distinguished Professor of English and Creative Writing at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Writers retreat. His third novel, The Road to the Country, was published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nRosie is a production and event manager based in Athens, Greece, with extensive experience in coordinating high-profile film festivals and cultural events. She holds a degree in Communication, Media and Culture from Athens and pursued further studies in Art History in Paris, culminating in a Master's in Culture & Tourism from Université Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne. Her professional experience includes collaborations with cultural organizations and festivals worldwide, including UNESCO in New York, the Rolex Art Festival, Les Rencontres d'Arles Photo Festival among others. Since 2018, she has served as Festival Coordinator and Special Events Manager for the French Film Festival of Greece, and since 2022, she has been the Head of Production for the Athens International Children's Film Festival. Driven by a deep passion for cultural engagement and sustainable tourism, she continually seeks innovative ways to connect communities through the arts. In her free time, she enjoys playing music and gardening.\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationaler Literaturpreis, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Professor of Creative Writing and English at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Fiction Writers program. His third novel, The Road to the Country, will be published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nKaterina Papanikolopoulos joined Faliro House in 2022 as Manager of Special Projects – a position that evolved into her role acting as the 2024 Oxbelly Retreat, Fiction Writers Program Manager. Following her graduation from UCLA (Summa Cum Laude, Art History), Papanikolopoulos founded the non-profit Athens Design Forum (ADF), a platform that advocates for overlooked and generative design histories interwoven with global labor and migration pa\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":3000,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_76bff0524f7149cca3bf0789"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d90\"},\"ref\":\"d90\",\"snippet\":\" ... Program Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationaler Literaturpreis, FT/Oppenheimer prize ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d77\"},\"ref\":\"d77\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2015 | Shortlist | Tom McCarthy | Satin Island | Jonathan Cape | * Michael Wood (chair) * John Burnside * Sam Leith * Frances Osborne * Ellah Wakatama Allfrey |\\n| 2015 | Shortlist | Chigozie Obioma | The Fishermen | One | * Michael Wood (chair) * John Burnside * Sam Leith * Frances Osborne * Ellah Wakatama Allfrey |\\n| 2015 | Shortlist | Sunjeev Sahota | The Year of the Runaways ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d133\"},\"ref\":\"d133\",\"snippet\":\" ... Arrow of God (1964), No Longer At Ease (1960), Things Fall Apart (1958), A Man of the People (1966), Anthills of the Savannah (1987), \\n* Chimamanda Ngozi Adichie (Nigeria): Purple Hibiscus (2003), Half of a Yellow Sun (2006), Americanah (2013)\\n* Chigozie Obioma (Nigeria): The Fishermen (2015), An Orchestra of ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d134\"},\"ref\":\"d134\",\"snippet\":\" ... This book brilliantly explores the effects of slavery and colonialism on African families as the story unfolds between West Africa and the United States.\\n\\n- The Fishermen (2015) by Chigozie Obioma (Nigeria): In this heartbreaking tale, four brothers in a small Nigerian town have their lives turned upside down ... \",\"title\":\"https://enkoeducation.com/the-must-read-in-african-literature/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"pr